{#- Formal verification report. Monochrome, print-friendly, no external assets, -#}
{#- because it is read on the script server or copied to a laptop offline.      -#}
{#- Companion to stage08-verification.md.j2 - same data, audit presentation.    -#}
{% set n_fail = dc_failed_rows | default([]) | length %}
{% set n_total = dc_total_checks | int %}
{% set n_pass = n_total - n_fail %}
{% set bgp_nv = dc_bgp_undetermined_rows | default([]) | length %}
{% set sub_nv = dc_subif_undetermined_rows | default([]) | length %}
{% set n_nv = bgp_nv + sub_nv %}
<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
<meta charset="utf-8">
<meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1">
<title>Intent Verification Report &mdash; Stage 08</title>
<style>
  :root { --ink:#1a1a1a; --muted:#5f6b76; --rule:#d5d9dd; --rule-strong:#9aa3ac; --shade:#f4f5f6; }
  * { box-sizing:border-box; }
  html { -webkit-text-size-adjust:100%; }
  body {
    margin:0; background:#fff; color:var(--ink);
    font:15px/1.6 "Segoe UI", Helvetica, Arial, sans-serif;
    font-variant-numeric:tabular-nums;
  }
  .page { max-width:960px; margin:0 auto; padding:56px 48px 72px; }
  a { color:inherit; text-decoration:none; border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule-strong); }
  a:hover { border-bottom-color:var(--ink); }

  .doc-title { font-size:26px; font-weight:600; letter-spacing:-.2px; margin:0; }
  .doc-sub { color:var(--muted); font-size:14px; margin:6px 0 0; }
  .rule { border:0; border-top:2px solid var(--ink); margin:20px 0 0; }

  h2 { font-size:15px; font-weight:600; letter-spacing:.08em; text-transform:uppercase;
       margin:44px 0 14px; padding-bottom:7px; border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule-strong); }
  h3 { font-size:15px; font-weight:600; margin:30px 0 10px; }
  p { margin:0 0 12px; }
  .muted { color:var(--muted); }
  .small { font-size:13px; }

  table { width:100%; border-collapse:collapse; margin:0 0 16px; font-size:14px; }
  caption { text-align:left; color:var(--muted); font-size:13px; padding-bottom:6px; }
  th, td { text-align:left; padding:7px 12px 7px 0; border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule);
           vertical-align:top; }
  thead th { border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule-strong); font-weight:600; font-size:12px;
             letter-spacing:.06em; text-transform:uppercase; color:var(--muted); }
  tbody tr:last-child td { border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule-strong); }
  td.status { white-space:nowrap; width:1%; padding-right:24px; }
  .exception td { background:var(--shade); }
  .exception td.status { font-weight:600; }

  code, .mono { font-family:ui-monospace, "SF Mono", Menlo, Consolas, monospace; font-size:13px; }
  code { background:none; padding:0; }

  dl.meta { display:grid; grid-template-columns:200px 1fr; gap:0; margin:0;
            border-top:1px solid var(--rule); font-size:14px; }
  dl.meta dt { padding:7px 0; color:var(--muted); border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule); }
  dl.meta dd { padding:7px 0; margin:0; border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule); }

  ol.toc { margin:0; padding-left:20px; font-size:14px; }
  ol.toc li { margin:4px 0; }
  ol.toc ol { padding-left:20px; margin:4px 0; }

  .statement { border-left:3px solid var(--ink); padding:2px 0 2px 16px; margin:0 0 18px;
               font-size:15px; }
  .backlink { font-size:12px; color:var(--muted); font-weight:400; letter-spacing:0;
              text-transform:none; margin-left:10px; }
  .backlink a { border-bottom:none; }
  footer { margin-top:48px; padding-top:14px; border-top:1px solid var(--rule);
           color:var(--muted); font-size:12px; }

  @media print {
    .page { padding:0; max-width:none; }
    a { border-bottom:none; }
    h2 { page-break-after:avoid; }
    table, tr { page-break-inside:avoid; }
    .toc-section { page-break-after:always; }
  }
</style>
</head>
<body>
<div class="page" id="top">

<p class="doc-title">Intent Verification Report</p>
<p class="doc-sub">Data centre VXLAN EVPN fabric &mdash; pipeline stage 08</p>
<hr class="rule">

<h2>Document control</h2>
<dl class="meta">
  <dt>Report generated</dt><dd>{{ dc_verify_timestamp }}</dd>
  <dt>Produced by</dt><dd><code>playbooks/08_verify_fabric.yml</code></dd>
  <dt>Fabric</dt><dd><code>{{ dc_fabric_name }}</code></dd>
  <dt>Controller</dt><dd><code>{{ ansible_host }}</code></dd>
  <dt>Intent sources</dt>
  <dd><code>group_vars/all/dc_switches.yml</code>, <code>group_vars/all/dc_vrf_lite.yml</code>,
      <code>host_vars/{{ inventory_hostname }}/vrfs.nac.yaml</code> and
      <code>host_vars/{{ inventory_hostname }}/networks.nac.yaml</code></dd>
  <dt>Evidence collection</dt>
  <dd>Nexus Dashboard REST over <code>httpapi</code>; border leaf read over SSH, with
      <code>show interface</code> parsed by pyATS/Genie</dd>
  <dt>Devices in scope</dt><dd>{{ dc_switch_rows | default([]) | length }}</dd>
  <dt>Controls evaluated</dt><dd>{{ n_total }}</dd>
  <dt>Assessment</dt>
  <dd>{% if n_fail > 0 %}Non-conformant &mdash; {{ n_fail }} exception(s){% else %}Conformant &mdash; no exceptions{% endif %}</dd>
</dl>

<h2>Contents</h2>
<div class="toc-section">
<ol class="toc">
  <li><a href="#s1">Conclusion</a></li>
  <li><a href="#s2">Scope</a></li>
  <li><a href="#s3">Basis of verification</a></li>
  <li><a href="#s4">Findings</a>
    <ol>
      <li><a href="#f1">Switches</a></li>
      <li><a href="#f2">VRFs</a></li>
      <li><a href="#f3">Networks</a></li>
      <li><a href="#f4">VRF-Lite extensions</a></li>
      <li><a href="#f5">VRF-Lite sub-interfaces</a></li>
      <li><a href="#f6">VRF-Lite BGP sessions</a></li>
    </ol>
  </li>
  <li><a href="#s5">Limitations of scope</a></li>
</ol>
</div>

<h2 id="s1">1. Conclusion</h2>
{% if n_fail > 0 %}
<p class="statement">
  The deployed fabric does <strong>not</strong> conform to the declared intent.
  {{ n_fail }} of {{ n_total }} evaluated controls returned an exception.
  Details are recorded in section 4.
</p>
{% else %}
<p class="statement">
  The deployed fabric conforms to the declared intent. All
  {{ n_pass }} evaluated controls passed, with no exceptions.
</p>
{% endif %}

<table>
  <caption>Table 1 &mdash; Summary of results</caption>
  <thead><tr><th>Outcome</th><th>Controls</th><th>Basis</th></tr></thead>
  <tbody>
    <tr><td>Pass</td><td>{{ n_pass }}</td>
        <td class="muted">Observed value equals the declared value</td></tr>
    <tr><td>Exception</td><td>{{ n_fail }}</td>
        <td class="muted">Observed value differs from the declared value</td></tr>
    <tr><td>Not verified</td><td>{{ n_nv }}</td>
        <td class="muted">The border leaf did not answer; no opinion expressed</td></tr>
  </tbody>
</table>

<h2 id="s2">2. Scope</h2>
<p>
  The switches below were assessed. Each is held in the Nexus Dashboard
  inventory for <code>{{ dc_fabric_name }}</code> and was addressed through the
  controller's API using its management address.
</p>
<table>
  <caption>Table 2 &mdash; Devices in scope</caption>
  <thead><tr><th>Management address</th><th>Switch</th><th>Serial</th><th>Role declared</th></tr></thead>
  <tbody>
  {% for row in dc_switch_rows | default([]) %}
    <tr><td class="mono">{{ row.ip }}</td><td class="mono">{{ row.name }}</td>
        <td class="mono">{{ row.serial }}</td><td>{{ row.declared_role }}</td></tr>
  {% endfor %}
  </tbody>
</table>

<h2 id="s3">3. Basis of verification</h2>
<p>
  Declared intent was taken from the repository, and observed state from two
  independent sources. Every finding except sections 4.5 and 4.6 is read from
  the Nexus Dashboard API, needs no device SSH, and is therefore valid even
  when the switch management addresses are unreachable from the host running
  this stage.
</p>
<p>
  Sections 4.5 and 4.6 are read from <code>{{ dc_vrf_lite_border_leaf }}</code>
  itself over SSH, because the controller holds no API that reports either the
  running configuration of a sub-interface or routing protocol state. Where
  that switch could not be reached, the affected controls are reported as
  <em>not verified</em> and excluded from the counts in section 1 rather than
  being recorded as failures.
</p>
<table>
  <caption>Table 3 &mdash; Evidence relied upon</caption>
  <thead><tr><th style="width:30%">Finding</th><th>Source</th><th>Method</th></tr></thead>
  <tbody>
    <tr><td>Switches</td><td class="mono">rest/control/fabrics/.../inventory</td><td>Controller API</td></tr>
    <tr><td>VRFs</td><td class="mono">rest/top-down/fabrics/.../vrfs</td><td>Controller API</td></tr>
    <tr><td>Networks</td><td class="mono">rest/top-down/fabrics/.../networks</td><td>Controller API</td></tr>
    <tr><td>VRF-Lite extensions</td><td class="mono">rest/top-down/fabrics/.../vrfs/switches</td><td>Controller API</td></tr>
    <tr><td>Sub-interfaces</td><td class="mono">show interface {{ dc_vrf_lite_interface }}.&lt;dot1q&gt;</td><td>SSH, parsed by pyATS/Genie</td></tr>
    <tr><td>BGP sessions</td><td class="mono">show bgp sessions vrf &lt;vrf&gt;</td><td>SSH, NX-OS JSON output</td></tr>
  </tbody>
</table>

<h2 id="s4">4. Findings</h2>
<p>
  Each row states one declared value and the corresponding value observed.
  Comparison is exact equality against a named field. Rows marked
  <strong>Exception</strong> are shaded.
</p>

<h3 id="f1">4.1 Switches
  <span class="backlink">{{ dc_switch_rows | default([]) | rejectattr('ok') | list | length }} exception(s) &middot; <a href="#top">top</a></span>
</h3>
<table>
  <caption>Table 4 &mdash; Inventory and role</caption>
  <thead><tr><th>Switch</th><th>Result</th><th>Role declared</th><th>Role observed</th><th>Mode</th><th>Compliance</th></tr></thead>
  <tbody>
  {% for row in dc_switch_rows | default([]) %}
    <tr{% if not row.ok %} class="exception"{% endif %}>
      <td class="mono">{{ row.name }}</td>
      <td class="status">{{ 'Pass' if row.ok else 'Exception' }}</td>
      <td>{{ row.declared_role }}</td><td>{{ row.observed_role }}</td>
      <td>{{ row.mode }}</td><td>{{ row.cc_status }}</td>
    </tr>
  {% endfor %}
  </tbody>
</table>
<p class="small muted">
  A switch raises an exception when Nexus Dashboard holds no inventory record at
  its management address, or when the role it carries is not the role declared
  for it.
</p>

<h3 id="f2">4.2 VRFs
  <span class="backlink">{{ dc_vrf_rows | default([]) | rejectattr('ok') | list | length }} exception(s) &middot; <a href="#top">top</a></span>
</h3>
<table>
  <caption>Table 5 &mdash; VRFs and their attachments</caption>
  <thead><tr><th>VRF</th><th>Result</th><th>VNI declared</th><th>VNI observed</th><th>Attached to</th><th>Missing</th><th>States</th></tr></thead>
  <tbody>
  {% for row in dc_vrf_rows | default([]) %}
    <tr{% if not row.ok %} class="exception"{% endif %}>
      <td class="mono">{{ row.name }}</td>
      <td class="status">{{ 'Pass' if row.ok else 'Exception' }}</td>
      <td class="mono">{{ row.declared_id }}</td><td class="mono">{{ row.observed_id }}</td>
      <td>{{ row.declared_switches | join(', ') if row.declared_switches else 'none' }}</td>
      <td>{{ row.missing_switches | join(', ') if row.missing_switches else 'none' }}</td>
      <td>{{ row.attach_states | join(', ') if row.attach_states else 'none' }}</td>
    </tr>
  {% endfor %}
  </tbody>
</table>
<p class="small muted">
  A VRF must exist with the declared VNI and be attached, in <code>DEPLOYED</code>,
  to every switch in its <code>vrf_attach_group</code>. An attachment stuck in
  <code>PENDING</code> means the intent was created but never pushed.
</p>

<h3 id="f3">4.3 Networks
  <span class="backlink">{{ dc_network_rows | default([]) | rejectattr('ok') | list | length }} exception(s) &middot; <a href="#top">top</a></span>
</h3>
<table>
  <caption>Table 6 &mdash; Networks, gateways and attachments</caption>
  <thead><tr><th>Network</th><th>Result</th><th>VRF</th><th>Gateway declared</th><th>Gateway observed</th><th>Missing attachments</th></tr></thead>
  <tbody>
  {% for row in dc_network_rows | default([]) %}
    <tr{% if not row.ok %} class="exception"{% endif %}>
      <td class="mono">{{ row.name }}</td>
      <td class="status">{{ 'Pass' if row.ok else 'Exception' }}</td>
      <td class="mono">{{ row.observed_vrf }}</td>
      <td class="mono">{{ row.declared_gateway }}</td><td class="mono">{{ row.observed_gateway }}</td>
      <td>{{ row.missing_attachments | map('replace', '|', ' ') | join(', ') if row.missing_attachments else 'none' }}</td>
    </tr>
  {% endfor %}
  </tbody>
</table>
<p class="small muted">
  Each declared port-channel must be attached on every switch it was declared
  on, with every attachment in <code>DEPLOYED</code>, so a network that reached
  one leaf but not its vPC peer raises an exception rather than passing.
</p>

<h3 id="f4">4.4 VRF-Lite extensions
  <span class="backlink">{{ dc_vrf_lite_rows | default([]) | rejectattr('ok') | list | length }} exception(s) &middot; <a href="#top">top</a></span>
</h3>
<table>
  <caption>Table 7 &mdash; Extensions held by the controller</caption>
  <thead><tr><th style="width:26%">Extension</th><th>Result</th><th>Declared</th><th>Attached</th><th>State</th></tr></thead>
  <tbody>
  {% for row in dc_vrf_lite_rows | default([]) %}
    <tr{% if not row.ok %} class="exception"{% endif %}>
      <td>{{ row.name }}</td>
      <td class="status">{{ 'Pass' if row.ok else 'Exception' }}</td>
      <td class="mono">{{ row.declared }}</td>
      <td>{{ 'yes' if row.attached else 'no' }}</td>
      <td>{{ row.state }}</td>
    </tr>
  {% endfor %}
  </tbody>
</table>
<p class="small muted">
  Each extension must be attached to the border leaf, in <code>DEPLOYED</code>,
  and its <code>extensionValues</code> must carry the declared interface, dot1q
  tag and neighbour address.
</p>

<h3 id="f5">4.5 VRF-Lite sub-interfaces
  <span class="backlink">{{ dc_subif_rows | default([]) | selectattr('determined') | rejectattr('ok') | list | length }} exception(s) &middot; <a href="#top">top</a></span>
</h3>
{% if dc_subif_rows | default([]) | selectattr('determined') | list %}
<table>
  <caption>Table 8 &mdash; Sub-interfaces as configured on {{ dc_vrf_lite_border_leaf }}</caption>
  <thead><tr><th style="width:26%">Sub-interface</th><th>Result</th><th>Declared</th><th>Oper</th><th>Dot1q</th><th>Address</th><th>MTU</th></tr></thead>
  <tbody>
  {% for row in dc_subif_rows | default([]) | selectattr('determined') %}
    <tr{% if not row.ok %} class="exception"{% endif %}>
      <td class="mono">{{ row.name }}</td>
      <td class="status">{{ 'Pass' if row.ok else 'Exception' }}</td>
      <td class="mono">{{ row.declared }}</td>
      <td>{{ row.oper_status }}</td>
      <td>{{ 'yes' if row.dot1q_ok else 'NO' }}</td>
      <td>{{ 'yes' if row.address_ok else 'NO' }}</td>
      <td>{{ 'yes' if row.mtu_ok else 'NO' }}</td>
    </tr>
  {% endfor %}
  </tbody>
</table>
<p class="small muted">
  Section 4.4 is what the controller believes; this is what the switch runs.
  Extensions <code>DEPLOYED</code> on the controller with no sub-interface here
  means the deploy did not reach the switch.
</p>
{% else %}
<p class="muted">
  Not verified. <code>{{ dc_vrf_lite_border_leaf }}</code> was not read, so none
  of the sub-interfaces were assessed.
</p>
{% endif %}

<h3 id="f6">4.6 VRF-Lite BGP sessions
  <span class="backlink">{{ dc_bgp_rows | default([]) | selectattr('determined') | rejectattr('ok') | list | length }} exception(s) &middot; <a href="#top">top</a></span>
</h3>
{% if not (dc_verify_bgp_sessions | bool) %}
<p class="muted">
  Not verified. This run was made with <code>-e dc_verify_bgp_sessions=false</code>,
  so the border leaf was not read.
</p>
{% elif not (dc_vrf_lite_rows | default([])) %}
<p class="muted">
  No VRF-Lite extensions are declared, so there are no sessions to assess.
</p>
{% else %}
<table>
  <caption>Table 9 &mdash; eBGP sessions observed on {{ dc_vrf_lite_border_leaf }}</caption>
  <thead><tr><th>VRF</th><th>Result</th><th>Neighbour</th><th>Peer ASN</th><th>State expected</th><th>State observed</th></tr></thead>
  <tbody>
  {% for row in dc_bgp_rows | default([]) %}
    <tr{% if row.determined and not row.ok %} class="exception"{% endif %}>
      <td class="mono">{{ row.vrf }}</td>
      <td class="status">{{ 'Not verified' if not row.determined else ('Pass' if row.ok else 'Exception') }}</td>
      <td class="mono">{{ row.neighbor }}</td>
      <td class="mono">{{ row.peer_as }}</td>
      <td>{{ row.expected_state }}</td>
      <td>{{ row.observed_state }}</td>
    </tr>
  {% endfor %}
  </tbody>
</table>
<p class="small muted">
  This is the only finding that describes the fabric rather than the
  controller's intent for it. <code>Established</code> is the only state that
  means external connectivity works. <code>Idle</code> and <code>Active</code>
  both point at the far end, whose side of these links is pre-built by the pod
  and which Nexus Dashboard never writes to.
</p>
{% endif %}

<h2 id="s5">5. Limitations of scope</h2>
{% if n_nv > 0 %}
<p>
  The controls below could not be evaluated, because
  <code>{{ dc_vrf_lite_border_leaf }}</code> did not answer:
  {{ dc_bgp_undetermined_reason }}. No opinion is expressed on them, and they
  are excluded from the counts in section 1.
</p>
<table>
  <caption>Table 10 &mdash; Controls not evaluated</caption>
  <thead><tr><th>Control</th><th>Reason</th></tr></thead>
  <tbody>
  {% for row in dc_subif_rows | default([]) | rejectattr('determined') %}
    <tr><td>{{ row.name }}</td><td class="muted">Sub-interface not read</td></tr>
  {% endfor %}
  {% for row in dc_bgp_rows | default([]) | rejectattr('determined') %}
    <tr><td>BGP session {{ row.vrf }} to {{ row.neighbor }}</td><td class="muted">Session state not read</td></tr>
  {% endfor %}
  </tbody>
</table>
{% else %}
<p class="muted">
  None. Every declared control was evaluated against observed evidence.
</p>
{% endif %}
<p class="small muted">
  Outside the scope of this report in all cases: the edge router's side of the
  VRF-Lite links, which is pre-built by the pod and which Nexus Dashboard never
  writes to; the fabric underlay and the EVPN overlay, since the session table
  covers only the three VRF-Lite eBGP sessions; and the data plane, since
  nothing here sends a packet between two workloads.
</p>

<footer>
  This assessment is read-only: it issues Nexus Dashboard GET requests and
  <code>show</code> commands only, and makes no change to any device.
  {{ n_total }} control(s) evaluated across
  {{ dc_switch_rows | default([]) | length }} switch(es) in
  <code>{{ dc_fabric_name }}</code>.
</footer>

</div>
</body>
</html>
